.TH ANNOTA 1 "October 2026" "annota 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
annota \- capture, mark up and record your screen
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B annota
[\fIOPTION\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Annota is a screenshot and annotation tool for GNOME. It runs as a single instance:
a second invocation forwards its request to the running instance.
Annota works entirely offline and never contacts a network service.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-capture\fR=\fIMODE\fR
Start a capture. \fIMODE\fR is one of \fBregion\fR, \fBwindow\fR or \fBscreen\fR.
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-delay\fR=\fISECONDS\fR
Delay the capture by 0 to 60 seconds.
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-open\fR=\fIFILE\fR
Open an image or \fI.annota\fR file in the editor.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Show the version and exit.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show help options.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 2 for invalid command-line usage.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/trosinde/Annota
